WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.839
-[rapid beeping]
-Run!

2
00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:09.009
-Run. run. run! Go. go!
-[Dale] I got an H2S leak

3
00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:11.744
at 5272. Send Hazmat and EMS.

4
00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.865
We're partners barely a month.
Look how well we're doing.

5
00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:17.535
Oh. no. you're not partners
with me.

6
00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:20.019
You're partners
with a 22-year-old kid.

7
00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.106
You bet on him to fail.

8
00:00:21.189 --> 00:00:22.390
so he would owe you.

9
00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.774
and so I'd owe you.
I don't owe you

10
00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:25.376
a fucking thing
and neither does he.

11
00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.943
Hey. every time you
take a fucking breath.

12
00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.278
-you owe me. Thomas.
-Really?

13
00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:30.431
Every time you take
a fucking breath!

14
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.000
[Cami] I now know why Monty
was so stressed.

15
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.835
The company has no money.

16
00:00:34.935 --> 00:00:36.621
You might want to hang here
for a minute. okay?

17
00:00:36.704 --> 00:00:37.787
Well. now. why would I do that?

18
00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.323
Because I'm-a get
a little rough.

19
00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:41.408
-[grunts]
-Come here.

20
00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.576
Who's the gangster now?

21
00:00:44.378 --> 00:00:45.862
It's like I'm looking
into a mirror.

22
00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.164
You ever bar tend before?

23
00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.415
Just for fun.

24
00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:49.567
You ain't gonna think
it's fun here.

25
00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.969
It could get interesting.

26
00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.470
Who died?

27
00:00:53.554 --> 00:00:54.921
My mother.

28
00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:56.441
[T.L.]
It's a disease. you know?

29
00:00:56.524 --> 00:00:58.725
And it killed a part
of her I loved.

30
00:00:58.859 --> 00:01:01.060
and left us with
the woman you knew.

31
00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:02.862
Funeral's Friday.

32
00:01:03.697 --> 00:01:05.698
♪ I got a little change
in my pocket ♪

33
00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.801
♪ Going "jing-a-ling-ling" ♪

34
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.237
♪ Want to call you
on the telephone. baby ♪

35
00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.305
♪ I give you a ring ♪

36
00:01:12.406 --> 00:01:14.108
♪ But each time we talk ♪

37
00:01:14.242 --> 00:01:15.975
♪ I get the same old thing ♪

38
00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.078
♪ Always.
"No huggee. no kissee ♪

39
00:01:18.212 --> 00:01:21.013
♪ Until I get a wedding ring" ♪

40
00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:24.652
♪ My honey. my baby. don't put
my love upon no shelf ♪

41
00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.254
♪ She said.
"Don't hand me no lines ♪

42
00:01:27.355 --> 00:01:29.656
♪ And keep your hands
to yourself" ♪

43
00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.049
♪ Ooh. baby. baby. baby ♪

44
00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:40.901
♪ Why you gonna treat me
this way? ♪

45
00:01:41.001 --> 00:01:43.436
♪ You know I'm still
your lover boy ♪

46
00:01:43.537 --> 00:01:45.103
♪ I still feel the same way ♪

47
00:01:45.206 --> 00:01:47.740
♪ That's when
she told me a story ♪

48
00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:49.576
♪ About free milk and a cow ♪

49
00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:52.111
♪ And said.
"No huggee. no kissee ♪

50
00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:54.347
♪ Until I get a wedding vow" ♪

51
00:01:54.448 --> 00:01:56.049
♪ My honey. my baby ♪

52
00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:57.801
♪ Don't put my love
upon no shelf ♪

53
00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.870
♪ She said.
"Don't hand me no lines ♪

54
00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:03.623
♪ And keep your hands
to yourself" ♪

55
00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.632
♪♪♪

56
00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.805
Shit!

57
00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.647
♪ Go. man. go! ♪

58
00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.090
♪♪♪

59
00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.543
♪ gentle music ♪

60
00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.569
♪♪♪

61
00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.930
♪♪♪

62
00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:02.443
♪ slow. somber music ♪

63
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.156
[lighter flicking]

64
00:04:21.528 --> 00:04:24.130
-Come out here for a smoke?
-[laughs softly]

65
00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.632
The opposite.

66
00:04:25.766 --> 00:04:28.000
Needed some fresh air.

67
00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.970
Yeah.

68
00:04:31.338 --> 00:04:32.689
How'd you finish out the night?

69
00:04:32.773 --> 00:04:34.408
Uh...

70
00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.310
Haven't counted yet.

71
00:04:36.444 --> 00:04:37.862
Don't count it out here.

72
00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:39.045
[chuckles]

73
00:04:39.146 --> 00:04:40.980
Count it in the office.

74
00:04:41.715 --> 00:04:43.850
I need to tip the bar backs?

75
00:04:43.951 --> 00:04:45.786
Twenty percent.

76
00:04:47.521 --> 00:04:49.590
So. what are you thinking. huh?

77
00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:52.326
-We gonna see you tomorrow?
-[scoffs]

78
00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:54.661
-It is tomorrow.
-[chuckles]

79
00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.630
Are we gonna see you today?

80
00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.502
I'm a single mother.

81
00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:05.221
I can't be getting home
at 5:00 in the morning

82
00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:08.576
to a baby who wakes at 7:00.

83
00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:09.910
Yeah.

84
00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:13.646
You know. I'd count that stack
before you say no.

85
00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.353
Two nights a week here is like

86
00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.889
two weeks of nights
anywhere else.

87
00:05:25.959 --> 00:05:27.827
Two nights a week I could do.

88
00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:31.831
I assume Friday and Saturday
are the best days?

89
00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:35.002
When oil's booming...
[chuckles]

90
00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.803
...it don't make no difference.

91
00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:38.838
[exhales sharply]

92
00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.173
Every night's Friday night.

93
00:05:43.043 --> 00:05:45.512
♪ Slow. gentle music ♪

94
00:05:48.449 --> 00:05:50.617
♪♪♪

95
00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:59.091
♪♪♪

96
00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:15.742
Cooper.

97
00:06:15.843 --> 00:06:17.778
What are you doing?

98
00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:19.447
[grunts]

99
00:06:20.312 --> 00:06:21.581
Uh...

100
00:06:21.682 --> 00:06:23.382
Came to get my coat?

101
00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:24.985
It's too hot for a coat.

102
00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:27.788
A dress coat. Or a sports coat.

103
00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:30.139
Why didn't you just get it?
You have a key.

104
00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:32.476
Well. you told me to leave.

105
00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.795
Didn't feel right going in your
house without your permission.

106
00:06:35.896 --> 00:06:38.731
But it felt right to sleep
on my porch like a stalker?

107
00:06:38.865 --> 00:06:40.901
I called you
and you didn't answer.

108
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.771
so I got worried.

109
00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:48.206
Come on in.

110
00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:50.143
[keys jingle]

111
00:06:50.242 --> 00:06:51.845
[lock clicking]

112
00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.625
[keys clatter]

113
00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:07.778
Are my things still in the...

114
00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.797
Still in the closet. Cooper.

115
00:07:10.831 --> 00:07:12.500
[fridge door closes]

116
00:07:26.613 --> 00:07:28.815
[water running]

117
00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:31.951
[inhales sharply]

118
00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.887
-[sighs]
-[water turns off]

119
00:07:38.091 --> 00:07:40.127
Uh. so. you're working
at the Patch?

120
00:07:40.226 --> 00:07:41.327
Mm-hmm.

121
00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:43.797
Supposed to be
a pretty rough place.

122
00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:45.865
Lives up to its reputation.

123
00:07:46.932 --> 00:07:48.268
What's with the coat?

124
00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:49.937
Big meeting?

125
00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:52.505
Uh. Grandmother died.

126
00:07:54.074 --> 00:07:57.276
Oh. Cooper. I'm so sorry.

127
00:07:57.377 --> 00:07:59.596
It's okay. I-I didn't know her.

128
00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.180
She had a troubled life.

129
00:08:01.281 --> 00:08:03.550
but still a funeral
all the same.

130
00:08:03.651 --> 00:08:06.653
-In town?
-In the Panhandle.

131
00:08:06.754 --> 00:08:08.454
Canadian.

132
00:08:08.555 --> 00:08:10.156
Is that far?

133
00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:12.291
It's a drive.

134
00:08:14.326 --> 00:08:16.163
Give me five minutes to change.

135
00:08:16.963 --> 00:08:19.432
You don't have to do that.
It's fine.

136
00:08:19.533 --> 00:08:21.968
You were there for me.

137
00:08:22.069 --> 00:08:23.870
I'll be there for you.

138
00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:27.139
Like I said.
I didn't know her to miss her.

139
00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:30.009
You don't want me to go?

140
00:08:34.447 --> 00:08:36.481
I want you everywhere.

141
00:08:38.183 --> 00:08:40.471
Then give me five minutes.

142
00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:42.822
♪ Slow. dramatic music ♪

143
00:08:49.461 --> 00:08:51.631
[water running]

144
00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:57.037
♪♪♪

145
00:09:22.062 --> 00:09:24.230
♪♪♪

146
00:09:48.355 --> 00:09:50.490
♪♪♪

147
00:10:00.267 --> 00:10:01.668
[sniffles]

148
00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:10.143
I thought you didn't
know her to miss her.

149
00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:12.611
It's not her I'm missing.

150
00:10:12.712 --> 00:10:14.114
[laughs softly]

151
00:10:15.548 --> 00:10:18.518
Didn't miss me enough to fight
for me. though. did you?

152
00:10:20.352 --> 00:10:22.022
You told me to leave and I left.

153
00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:23.724
That's exactly what I meant.

154
00:10:25.759 --> 00:10:28.378
If you didn't want me to leave.
then why did you tell me to go?

155
00:10:28.461 --> 00:10:30.379
Because the only option
you were offering

156
00:10:30.462 --> 00:10:32.700
was me completely
uprooting my life.

157
00:10:32.799 --> 00:10:35.335
Leaving my home. my family.

158
00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:39.639
everything I've ever known
because you made some money.

159
00:10:40.908 --> 00:10:42.225
Hasn't occurred to you
to come up

160
00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:44.010
with another option. has it?

161
00:10:46.546 --> 00:10:48.347
So you left.

162
00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:52.085
You left.

163
00:10:53.253 --> 00:10:55.154
♪ Slow. somber music ♪

164
00:10:55.254 --> 00:10:57.557
How far is the drive
to Canadian?

165
00:10:58.390 --> 00:10:59.459
Seven hours.

166
00:10:59.558 --> 00:11:01.327
Wake me in five.

167
00:11:05.498 --> 00:11:06.866
[door opens]

168
00:11:07.167 --> 00:11:09.336
♪♪♪

169
00:11:27.754 --> 00:11:29.722
Y'all got court?

170
00:11:30.557 --> 00:11:31.792
We're going with you.

171
00:11:31.892 --> 00:11:33.442
Well. hell.
y'all don't even know her.

172
00:11:33.525 --> 00:11:35.913
-We ain't going for her. amigo.
-Well. I appreciate it.

173
00:11:35.995 --> 00:11:37.947
but I don't even know
why I'm going myself.

174
00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:39.081
to tell you the truth.

175
00:11:39.164 --> 00:11:40.384
[Angela]
Don't you boys look nice?

176
00:11:40.466 --> 00:11:41.533
Look at you. Dale.

177
00:11:41.668 --> 00:11:43.120
Told you a little fruit
and yogurt

178
00:11:43.202 --> 00:11:44.754
-would melt that fat away.
-[Dale] Yes. ma'am.

179
00:11:44.837 --> 00:11:46.139
You been working out. too?

180
00:11:46.239 --> 00:11:47.758
Uh. no. ma'am.
I've been taking Adderall.

181
00:11:47.841 --> 00:11:49.576
With these 20-hour days.
this coffee

182
00:11:49.709 --> 00:11:51.227
-just ain't fucking cutting it.
-[Tommy] Who knew

183
00:11:51.311 --> 00:11:53.245
the health benefits
of amphetamines?

184
00:11:53.379 --> 00:11:54.547
It's not amphetamine.

185
00:11:54.647 --> 00:11:55.381
-That's all it is.
-[Angela] Well.

186
00:11:55.481 --> 00:11:56.582
it's working.

187
00:11:56.682 --> 00:11:58.001
-so good for you.
-[Dale] Thank you.

188
00:11:58.085 --> 00:11:59.503
-Hey. baby. Y'all ready to go?
-Morning.

189
00:11:59.586 --> 00:12:00.888
-Let's go.
-You. uh.

190
00:12:00.988 --> 00:12:02.139
you want to ride with me?

191
00:12:02.221 --> 00:12:03.823
We'll all fit in the Expedition.

192
00:12:03.923 --> 00:12:06.143
Oh. good. Five of us
in the same car for seven hours.

193
00:12:06.225 --> 00:12:07.494
That's gonna be fun.

194
00:12:07.594 --> 00:12:09.245
Well. it could be
if you let it. Daddy.

195
00:12:09.328 --> 00:12:10.647
Sweetheart.
we're driving up through

196
00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.799
the Panhandle of Texas
to a funeral.

197
00:12:12.899 --> 00:12:15.201
That makes it
impossible to be fun.

198
00:12:15.302 --> 00:12:17.437
Only with that attitude.

199
00:12:17.537 --> 00:12:20.190
Tommy. you want me to drive?
I am very focused right now.

200
00:12:20.273 --> 00:12:21.640
[door opens]

201
00:12:22.408 --> 00:12:23.659
[Rebecca]
Wait. what happened?

202
00:12:23.743 --> 00:12:26.178
[Walt]
We're still piecing it together.

203
00:12:28.315 --> 00:12:30.167
One of your drivers
ran into a pickup

204
00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.201
parked on the easement
to your well.

205
00:12:32.284 --> 00:12:35.121
What. wait. who was parked
on our easement?

206
00:12:35.221 --> 00:12:37.756
Not sure. Ain't got him out yet.

207
00:12:37.857 --> 00:12:39.408
There's a chance
he was already dead

208
00:12:39.491 --> 00:12:40.793
when your man hit him.

209
00:12:40.894 --> 00:12:43.363
which is a good thing for you.
I would imagine.

210
00:12:43.462 --> 00:12:45.432
Your driver. however...

211
00:12:45.565 --> 00:12:46.799
did not survive.

212
00:12:46.933 --> 00:12:49.436
-and that's not good.
-[sighs]

213
00:12:49.568 --> 00:12:52.004
No. I would say it's not.

214
00:12:53.974 --> 00:12:55.375
Great.

215
00:12:55.475 --> 00:12:56.692
I got to go.

216
00:12:56.775 --> 00:12:58.278
I'll call you when I land.

217
00:13:05.284 --> 00:13:06.953
Hi.

218
00:13:07.053 --> 00:13:09.288
-You mind?
-[Charlie] Oh. Yeah. well...

219
00:13:09.389 --> 00:13:11.875
Wouldn't matter much if I did.
It's not my-my plane.

220
00:13:11.958 --> 00:13:13.994
Here. have a seat.
[clears throat]

221
00:13:15.195 --> 00:13:17.547
It's pretty windy. so if
you want a drink. get it now.

222
00:13:17.629 --> 00:13:19.149
Once we're in the air.
we're gonna need everyone

223
00:13:19.231 --> 00:13:21.184
to remain seated
with their seat belts on.

224
00:13:21.268 --> 00:13:23.921
-Came prepared.
-Uh. define "pretty windy."

225
00:13:24.004 --> 00:13:25.471
Gusts up to 70.

226
00:13:28.607 --> 00:13:30.110
Great.

227
00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:32.178
Nervous flyer?

228
00:13:32.278 --> 00:13:34.914
I have control issues

229
00:13:35.014 --> 00:13:38.150
that can manifest
in certain circumstances.

230
00:13:40.019 --> 00:13:41.571
Flying is one of them.

231
00:13:41.653 --> 00:13:44.823
♪ "Wolf Song"
by Andrew Lockington playing ♪

232
00:13:47.894 --> 00:13:52.198
♪ Long. long ride
on another day ♪

233
00:13:56.568 --> 00:14:00.740
♪ Come alive on another day ♪

234
00:14:05.312 --> 00:14:09.581
♪ Know that I don't run
a little. know why? ♪

235
00:14:16.956 --> 00:14:19.859
♪♪♪

236
00:14:23.863 --> 00:14:25.465
♪♪♪

237
00:14:29.135 --> 00:14:31.270
♪♪♪

238
00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.659
♪♪♪

239
00:15:05.605 --> 00:15:07.774
♪♪♪

240
00:15:30.363 --> 00:15:32.499
♪♪♪

241
00:15:39.272 --> 00:15:41.039
[exhales]

242
00:15:43.076 --> 00:15:44.977
[sighs]

243
00:15:45.077 --> 00:15:46.846
Oh. Monty.

244
00:15:48.215 --> 00:15:52.152
I am trying very hard
not to be mad at you.

245
00:15:53.519 --> 00:15:56.623
Focusing on the futility of it.

246
00:15:58.789 --> 00:16:01.827
My therapist thinks
I should write you a letter.

247
00:16:01.927 --> 00:16:04.831
Who knows? Maybe I will.

248
00:16:06.232 --> 00:16:07.833
Brought you a few things.

249
00:16:07.933 --> 00:16:09.902
[sniffles]

250
00:16:10.636 --> 00:16:12.255
Uh...
[chuckles]

251
00:16:12.339 --> 00:16:13.972
Your favorite.

252
00:16:15.008 --> 00:16:17.226
Harder to get
than I would have imagined.

253
00:16:17.309 --> 00:16:20.480
You didn't mention
they're illegal.

254
00:16:24.317 --> 00:16:26.286
[sniffles]
And...

255
00:16:26.385 --> 00:16:27.986
[chuckles]

256
00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:32.192
You can have this again.

257
00:16:32.325 --> 00:16:35.995
but they have a rule that. uh.

258
00:16:36.129 --> 00:16:38.298
you can't leave the bottle.

259
00:16:38.398 --> 00:16:42.568
So you're gonna have
to drink it all now.

260
00:16:43.403 --> 00:16:44.903
[sniffles]

261
00:16:49.609 --> 00:16:51.211
[exhales]

262
00:16:58.451 --> 00:17:00.820
I found this in your closet.

263
00:17:01.653 --> 00:17:03.423
Thank you.

264
00:17:04.289 --> 00:17:07.460
Oh. Monty. the 30th anniversary.

265
00:17:07.559 --> 00:17:09.929
♪ Slow. somber music ♪

266
00:17:10.028 --> 00:17:12.699
I thought we'd have 20 more.

267
00:17:36.756 --> 00:17:38.924
♪♪♪

268
00:18:03.215 --> 00:18:06.118
-[airplane rattling]
-What the hell is that?

269
00:18:06.252 --> 00:18:08.505
It's called
a TRT standing takeoff.

270
00:18:08.587 --> 00:18:09.939
It's because of the headwind.

271
00:18:10.021 --> 00:18:11.474
They do it a lot
on shorter runways.

272
00:18:11.557 --> 00:18:14.926
You. uh. you're probably
gonna feel a bit of a jolt.

273
00:18:17.096 --> 00:18:19.298
[high-pitched whirring]

274
00:18:21.867 --> 00:18:24.836
[shrieks]
What the fuck? Oh. my God!

275
00:18:27.773 --> 00:18:30.410
[shrieks]
Oh. my God!

276
00:18:34.846 --> 00:18:36.648
[gasping]
Oh. my God!

277
00:18:36.749 --> 00:18:38.651
Oh. my God.
[shrieking]

278
00:18:40.752 --> 00:18:42.989
I'm sorry!
[shrieking]

279
00:18:45.392 --> 00:18:46.375
Please. God.

280
00:18:46.459 --> 00:18:47.894
Hey. hey. hey. hey.

281
00:18:47.993 --> 00:18:49.362
Look at me. look at me.

282
00:18:49.461 --> 00:18:51.072
This is not how we die.
All right?

283
00:18:51.163 --> 00:18:52.382
-Okay.
-Now I need you to grab my knee

284
00:18:52.464 --> 00:18:54.017
and squeeze
the hell out of that.

285
00:18:54.099 --> 00:18:55.419
-All right?
-Your hand is fine.

286
00:18:55.501 --> 00:18:57.019
No. no. no.
I need you to grab my knee

287
00:18:57.103 --> 00:18:59.021
because I'm pretty sure
you've broken my hand.

288
00:18:59.105 --> 00:19:01.090
-Oh. I'm sorry.
-All right. there you go.

289
00:19:01.173 --> 00:19:02.541
-[shrieking]
-Hey...

290
00:19:04.611 --> 00:19:06.613
It's okay.

291
00:19:13.353 --> 00:19:15.355
-There we go.
-[sighs]

292
00:19:15.488 --> 00:19:18.490
-[laughs]
-[panting]

293
00:19:21.093 --> 00:19:24.130
[panting. sighs]

294
00:19:29.602 --> 00:19:30.819
Everybody okay back here?

295
00:19:30.903 --> 00:19:33.138
Yeah? Okay?

296
00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:35.541
Okay. should be smooth
until our descent.

297
00:19:36.343 --> 00:19:37.777
Until our descent?

298
00:19:41.548 --> 00:19:44.768
So. how about that drink?

299
00:19:44.851 --> 00:19:46.152
-Please.
-Great.

300
00:19:48.555 --> 00:19:50.155
There.

301
00:19:55.528 --> 00:19:57.096
Hmm. What is this?

302
00:19:57.195 --> 00:20:00.967
That is vodka
and watermelon juice.

303
00:20:01.067 --> 00:20:03.220
-It's pretty good. right?
-Yeah. this is dangerous.

304
00:20:03.303 --> 00:20:05.471
Mm. I add simple syrup.

305
00:20:05.571 --> 00:20:07.906
Hmm. Because vodka
and fruit juice alone

306
00:20:08.007 --> 00:20:09.909
doesn't create
a bad enough hangover?

307
00:20:10.041 --> 00:20:11.243
A hangover?

308
00:20:11.377 --> 00:20:12.890
I work in the oil fields. miss.

309
00:20:12.979 --> 00:20:14.814
We sweat out
the hangover by noon.

310
00:20:14.913 --> 00:20:16.316
[Rebecca sighs]

311
00:20:16.415 --> 00:20:17.967
You think the turbulence
will be the same when we land?

312
00:20:18.049 --> 00:20:19.969
It's the same wind
blowing through Midland.

313
00:20:20.051 --> 00:20:23.154
I'm sorry to say.
just blowing harder.

314
00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:27.420
♪ "Hard Luck & Circumstances"
by Charley Crockett playing ♪

315
00:20:32.265 --> 00:20:34.800
-Mm.
-Oh. very good.

316
00:20:34.901 --> 00:20:36.536
That's the spirit.

317
00:20:36.635 --> 00:20:38.570
♪ When it comes to bad luck ♪

318
00:20:38.671 --> 00:20:41.874
♪ I got perfect timing ♪

319
00:20:42.575 --> 00:20:45.744
♪ All the stars just align ♪

320
00:20:48.146 --> 00:20:50.165
♪ Me and trouble ♪

321
00:20:50.249 --> 00:20:53.051
♪ We're old friends ♪

322
00:20:53.786 --> 00:20:56.873
♪ We understand
each other fine ♪

323
00:20:56.955 --> 00:21:00.527
[cutting out]
♪ Because it's hard ♪

324
00:21:01.361 --> 00:21:02.929
The music stopped.

325
00:21:03.028 --> 00:21:05.298
Ain't no cell service
out here. honey.

326
00:21:05.397 --> 00:21:08.099
-What about the regular radio?
-It's right here.

327
00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:10.502
-[static crackling]
-See that?

328
00:21:11.703 --> 00:21:13.940
[sighs]
People wonder why I left.

329
00:21:14.039 --> 00:21:15.625
No. they don't wonder
why you left. honey.

330
00:21:15.708 --> 00:21:18.310
-They wonder why you came back.
-Well. not to worry.

331
00:21:18.411 --> 00:21:20.813
I have plenty of road trip
playlists.

332
00:21:20.946 --> 00:21:22.815
What are y'all
in the mood for. huh?

333
00:21:22.914 --> 00:21:24.817
-Ooh.
-Okay. I've got yacht rock.

334
00:21:24.916 --> 00:21:26.618
sexy salsa.

335
00:21:26.719 --> 00:21:28.355
You know. it's like. um...

336
00:21:28.454 --> 00:21:30.273
-♪ Havana. oh. na-na. mm. mm ♪
-[fingers snapping]

337
00:21:30.356 --> 00:21:33.076
♪ Half of my heart
is in Havana. oh. na-na ♪

338
00:21:33.159 --> 00:21:34.510
-"Oh. na-na."
-How do you know that song?

339
00:21:34.594 --> 00:21:36.546
[Angela]
That's what it is.

340
00:21:36.628 --> 00:21:38.330
[sighs]
Geez.

341
00:21:38.431 --> 00:21:41.299
Look at you
sad Sallys in the back.

342
00:21:41.433 --> 00:21:43.802
Honey. we're driving
to a fucking funeral.

343
00:21:43.935 --> 00:21:46.172
I know where we're going.

344
00:21:46.271 --> 00:21:48.613
It doesn't mean that the drive
can't be pleasant.

345
00:21:48.708 --> 00:21:49.875
It can't be pleasant!

346
00:21:49.976 --> 00:21:51.810
We're driving
to a fucking funeral!

347
00:21:51.911 --> 00:21:54.063
If you're not careful.
they're gonna be burying

348
00:21:54.145 --> 00:21:55.332
someone else
at that son of a bitch.

349
00:21:55.414 --> 00:21:57.115
you talk to me like that.

350
00:21:57.950 --> 00:21:59.151
[exhales]
Okay.

351
00:21:59.285 --> 00:22:00.653
Yacht rock it is.

352
00:22:00.787 --> 00:22:02.855
[stifled laugh]

353
00:22:05.057 --> 00:22:06.476
Oh. do you find something funny?

354
00:22:06.558 --> 00:22:10.028
It is the antithesis
of humor. Angela.

355
00:22:10.162 --> 00:22:12.582
I don't know
how to explain what it is.

356
00:22:12.664 --> 00:22:14.866
Well. why don't you try. Neil?

357
00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:16.167
-Nate.
-I know what

358
00:22:16.301 --> 00:22:17.753
your fucking name is. okay?

359
00:22:17.836 --> 00:22:19.188
And after
you've explained yourself.

360
00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:20.539
maybe I'll use it.

361
00:22:20.673 --> 00:22:23.426
Maybe I'll choose
another fucking name for you.

362
00:22:23.509 --> 00:22:27.096
I don't think you should
explain what it is. Nate.

363
00:22:27.179 --> 00:22:29.481
It's a trap. Neil.

364
00:22:29.582 --> 00:22:31.182
I'm waiting.

365
00:22:32.818 --> 00:22:35.471
Yacht rock
would be my preference.

366
00:22:35.555 --> 00:22:38.223
[Angela] Well. it's your lucky
fucking day. Neil.

367
00:22:39.057 --> 00:22:41.644
♪ Oh. the canvas
can do miracles... ♪

368
00:22:41.728 --> 00:22:43.947
What? I mean.
I'm driving you to smoke?

369
00:22:44.029 --> 00:22:45.382
No. you're driving me
to suck Freon

370
00:22:45.464 --> 00:22:46.615
out of the back of an AC unit.

371
00:22:46.699 --> 00:22:49.268
-I'm settling for a cigarette.
-Fine.

372
00:22:49.367 --> 00:22:52.104
We'll all just be miserable
for the whole fucking day.

373
00:22:52.203 --> 00:22:53.204
[sighs]

374
00:22:53.338 --> 00:22:55.442
♪ Sailing ♪

375
00:22:55.541 --> 00:22:57.375
♪ Takes me away ♪

376
00:22:57.509 --> 00:22:59.878
♪ To where I've always ♪

377
00:22:59.979 --> 00:23:02.548
♪ Heard it could be ♪

378
00:23:03.281 --> 00:23:05.250
♪ gentle. pensive music

379
00:23:05.384 --> 00:23:08.386
[train horn blowing]

380
00:23:25.538 --> 00:23:27.673
♪♪♪

381
00:23:41.453 --> 00:23:43.707
[Cooper]
Hi. Uh. Mr. Norris?

382
00:23:43.789 --> 00:23:45.391
Thanks.

383
00:23:47.993 --> 00:23:49.028
Hey. Grandpa.

384
00:23:49.127 --> 00:23:50.997
Cooper.

385
00:23:53.298 --> 00:23:54.534
That ain't your sister.

386
00:23:54.634 --> 00:23:56.802
No. sir.

387
00:23:56.903 --> 00:23:58.505
I'm Ariana.

388
00:23:58.605 --> 00:23:59.971
Thomas.

389
00:24:00.071 --> 00:24:02.340
I'm so sorry
for your loss. Thomas.

390
00:24:02.441 --> 00:24:05.010
Oh. honey. I lost her years ago.

391
00:24:05.111 --> 00:24:08.146
Today. I'm just saying goodbye.

392
00:24:08.247 --> 00:24:09.582
Sit down.

393
00:24:13.986 --> 00:24:16.489
You're prettier
than he deserves.

394
00:24:16.623 --> 00:24:18.057
[chuckles softly]

395
00:24:18.156 --> 00:24:19.491
He doesn't have me.

396
00:24:19.592 --> 00:24:20.943
-No?
-Mm-mm.

397
00:24:21.027 --> 00:24:23.863
Mm. You're in the habit
of taking six-hour drives

398
00:24:23.996 --> 00:24:26.615
to funerals for people
you don't know

399
00:24:26.699 --> 00:24:28.267
with men you don't like?

400
00:24:28.366 --> 00:24:29.836
This is a first.

401
00:24:29.969 --> 00:24:32.171
[soft laughter]

402
00:24:33.005 --> 00:24:34.941
Smarter than you deserve. too.

403
00:24:36.976 --> 00:24:40.346
You don't even know what game
you're playing. do you?

404
00:24:40.445 --> 00:24:42.432
If you'd clue me in.
I'd sure appreciate it.

405
00:24:42.515 --> 00:24:43.982
Got to ask her.

406
00:24:44.083 --> 00:24:45.718
Play your cards right.

407
00:24:45.817 --> 00:24:48.186
she might even
tell you the rules.

408
00:24:48.287 --> 00:24:50.522
Of course.
she's gonna change them.

409
00:24:50.623 --> 00:24:52.858
At least you'll know
what they used to be.

410
00:24:52.991 --> 00:24:55.260
[laughs softly]

411
00:24:56.962 --> 00:25:00.148
This ain't your first rodeo
with one of these. is it?

412
00:25:00.231 --> 00:25:02.401
This is my fifth rodeo.

413
00:25:03.201 --> 00:25:05.203
If we're keeping count.

414
00:25:06.071 --> 00:25:09.240
Time comes there's
been too many to count.

415
00:25:10.009 --> 00:25:12.211
-That's where I am.
-[door opens]

416
00:25:17.048 --> 00:25:19.117
What are they putting
in your water?

417
00:25:19.218 --> 00:25:20.553
Hi. TL.

418
00:25:20.686 --> 00:25:22.354
You don't age.

419
00:25:24.155 --> 00:25:26.224
Mm...

420
00:25:26.325 --> 00:25:28.059
I'm so sorry. baby.

421
00:25:31.497 --> 00:25:32.832
Ainsley?

422
00:25:32.932 --> 00:25:34.432
Hi. Grandpa.

423
00:25:34.567 --> 00:25:36.635
Last time I saw you.
you were that big.

424
00:25:38.336 --> 00:25:41.073
Now it's like
a sunflower come to life.

425
00:25:41.874 --> 00:25:43.843
Who are these fucking clowns?

426
00:25:43.942 --> 00:25:45.778
[clears throat]
Uh. Dale. sir.

427
00:25:45.912 --> 00:25:47.896
That weren't a question
I expect you to answer.

428
00:25:47.980 --> 00:25:49.582
They work with me. Pop.

429
00:25:49.682 --> 00:25:51.584
Here for emotional support.
I expect.

430
00:25:51.718 --> 00:25:53.118
Yeah. something like that.

431
00:25:53.251 --> 00:25:55.121
As if you loved her enough
to need it.

432
00:25:55.253 --> 00:25:56.855
As if there's anything to love.

433
00:25:56.955 --> 00:25:58.207
Let's not get all misty

434
00:25:58.289 --> 00:26:00.192
and forget
who we're burying. all right?

435
00:26:03.494 --> 00:26:06.198
Let's get this over with.

436
00:26:12.171 --> 00:26:14.440
♪ Slow. somber music ♪

437
00:26:22.381 --> 00:26:24.583
♪♪♪

438
00:26:53.311 --> 00:26:55.480
♪♪♪

439
00:27:08.961 --> 00:27:12.030
[pastor]
From Psalm 34:18.

440
00:27:12.131 --> 00:27:15.701
"The Lord is near
to the brokenhearted

441
00:27:15.835 --> 00:27:18.170
and to the crushed in spirit."

442
00:27:18.304 --> 00:27:21.373
Dottie's life was troubled.

443
00:27:21.507 --> 00:27:23.875
but she has at last found peace.

444
00:27:24.643 --> 00:27:27.546
I'd like to offer her husband
an opportunity

445
00:27:27.680 --> 00:27:29.214
to offer a few words.

446
00:27:30.016 --> 00:27:32.969
Mr. Norris. is there anything
you'd like to say?

447
00:27:33.051 --> 00:27:34.653
Not to you.

448
00:27:35.354 --> 00:27:37.455
It's not to me. it's to God.

449
00:27:37.556 --> 00:27:40.058
God already knows it.

450
00:27:44.563 --> 00:27:46.449
The Lord is my shepherd.

451
00:27:46.531 --> 00:27:48.768
I shall not want.

452
00:27:49.801 --> 00:27:53.138
He maketh me
to lie in green pastures.

453
00:27:53.905 --> 00:27:57.409
He leadeth me to sit
beside still waters.

454
00:27:58.243 --> 00:28:00.346
He leadeth me...

455
00:28:01.180 --> 00:28:03.816
...in the paths of righteousness

456
00:28:03.915 --> 00:28:05.334
in His name.

457
00:28:05.416 --> 00:28:07.318
♪ Gentle. atmospheric music ♪

458
00:28:17.395 --> 00:28:19.147
[dishes clattering softly]

459
00:28:19.230 --> 00:28:21.400
[waitress]
Chicken-fried steaks.

460
00:28:23.335 --> 00:28:25.270
I have two chicken
Caesar salads.

461
00:28:25.403 --> 00:28:27.155
no dressing. no cheese

462
00:28:27.239 --> 00:28:29.174
-and no croutons.
-It's me.

463
00:28:29.275 --> 00:28:30.326
You don't say.

464
00:28:30.409 --> 00:28:31.743
Right here with the other.

465
00:28:31.877 --> 00:28:33.762
You realize that's just
lettuce and chicken?

466
00:28:33.846 --> 00:28:35.781
-I do.
-Cancer?

467
00:28:35.882 --> 00:28:37.333
Vanity.

468
00:28:37.415 --> 00:28:39.085
I'll pray for you.

469
00:28:39.184 --> 00:28:41.252
-Thank you.
-Homemade corn dogs?

470
00:28:41.353 --> 00:28:44.022
Here. Thank you.

471
00:28:44.123 --> 00:28:46.625
You got two corn dogs
for lunch. Pop?

472
00:28:46.759 --> 00:28:48.426
Best thing on the menu.

473
00:28:49.494 --> 00:28:51.348
-Thank you.
-[waitress] You're welcome.

474
00:28:54.800 --> 00:28:56.969
[T.L.]
Mmm.

475
00:29:06.278 --> 00:29:07.696
T.L.. how do you like your home?

476
00:29:07.779 --> 00:29:10.398
[chuckles]
It's not my home.

477
00:29:10.481 --> 00:29:14.220
It's an old Motel 6
they converted into a place

478
00:29:14.319 --> 00:29:16.321
where we wait to die.

479
00:29:16.422 --> 00:29:18.289
Fire took my home.

480
00:29:18.390 --> 00:29:19.791
Your house burned?

481
00:29:19.925 --> 00:29:22.077
Whole Panhandle burned.

482
00:29:22.161 --> 00:29:23.494
Well. from what?

483
00:29:23.595 --> 00:29:25.564
Same thing that always burns it.

484
00:29:25.663 --> 00:29:28.968
Drought. 70-mile-an-hour winds.

485
00:29:29.067 --> 00:29:31.386
fucking power line
on a pumpjack.

486
00:29:31.470 --> 00:29:32.788
Yeah. they need to bury them.

487
00:29:32.872 --> 00:29:34.472
You know how much that'd cost?

488
00:29:34.573 --> 00:29:36.058
You know how much
that fire cost?

489
00:29:36.142 --> 00:29:39.561
How many generations
of ranchers was wiped out?

490
00:29:39.644 --> 00:29:41.029
Oh. I'm not defending it. Pop.

491
00:29:41.113 --> 00:29:42.731
I'm just saying
that's why they don't do it.

492
00:29:42.815 --> 00:29:44.000
[T.L.]
Money is the reason.

493
00:29:44.083 --> 00:29:45.367
[Tommy]
It's always the reason.

494
00:29:45.451 --> 00:29:47.486
How come nobody's
talking about her?

495
00:29:50.155 --> 00:29:52.490
I've been to a few of these.

496
00:29:52.590 --> 00:29:55.693
You lay them to rest.
say goodbye.

497
00:29:55.827 --> 00:29:58.630
have a feast and...

498
00:29:59.397 --> 00:30:01.232
...talk about them.

499
00:30:02.667 --> 00:30:05.037
Remember what they meant to you?

500
00:30:08.840 --> 00:30:10.576
She was your mother. right?

501
00:30:12.211 --> 00:30:14.712
I don't have any memories
worth sharing.

502
00:30:17.148 --> 00:30:18.616
[clears throat]

503
00:30:25.958 --> 00:30:28.477
All right. here's one.
since you're so curious.

504
00:30:28.559 --> 00:30:29.728
Tommy.

505
00:30:29.827 --> 00:30:32.364
I remember
coming home from school...

506
00:30:34.465 --> 00:30:38.237
...and finding her naked.
face down in the bathtub.

507
00:30:39.704 --> 00:30:42.040
I was 14 years old.

508
00:30:43.142 --> 00:30:47.078
Dad. he was working on
the offshore rigs in Louisiana.

509
00:30:49.214 --> 00:30:51.150
I pulled her out by the hair...

510
00:30:51.917 --> 00:30:55.354
...and I called the ambulance.
and they walked me through CPR

511
00:30:55.453 --> 00:30:58.340
till she puked water in my face

512
00:30:58.423 --> 00:31:01.426
while I was blowing air
in her lungs.

513
00:31:04.195 --> 00:31:06.464
And she sat up...

514
00:31:07.298 --> 00:31:11.470
...and she looked at me
like I was a stranger.

515
00:31:15.207 --> 00:31:18.109
And then she pulled
her leg back...

516
00:31:19.444 --> 00:31:23.214
...and she kicked my nose
through the back of my head.

517
00:31:26.884 --> 00:31:29.121
Then she got up
and walked into the kitchen

518
00:31:29.255 --> 00:31:32.391
and made herself
another fucking drink.

519
00:31:36.427 --> 00:31:38.998
I went and put everything
I owned into a backpack.

520
00:31:39.097 --> 00:31:41.549
'cause a backpack's all it took.

521
00:31:41.633 --> 00:31:44.302
Never been back
in this town since...

522
00:31:45.104 --> 00:31:46.837
...till a week ago.

523
00:31:49.340 --> 00:31:51.609
There was no miracle
involving my mother

524
00:31:51.742 --> 00:31:55.314
other than her managing
to die of old age.

525
00:32:01.420 --> 00:32:03.788
And he was too weak
to leave her.

526
00:32:07.960 --> 00:32:09.795
So I left all of them.

527
00:32:13.898 --> 00:32:17.669
I didn't come here to
mourn her passing. honey. I...

528
00:32:17.769 --> 00:32:20.439
I came here to celebrate it.

529
00:32:31.416 --> 00:32:33.019
[sighs]

530
00:32:33.118 --> 00:32:34.819
I'll be in the car.

531
00:32:34.920 --> 00:32:36.538
Here you go. Pop.
Sort through that.

532
00:32:36.622 --> 00:32:38.085
That ought to take care of it.

533
00:32:44.130 --> 00:32:45.564
[clears throat]

534
00:32:47.833 --> 00:32:48.866
[door opens]

535
00:32:48.967 --> 00:32:51.869
I can tell you why...

536
00:32:52.003 --> 00:32:53.038
[door closes]

537
00:32:53.172 --> 00:32:55.340
What killed her soul.

538
00:32:56.174 --> 00:32:58.943
But it don't really matter now.
I guess.

539
00:33:00.778 --> 00:33:02.114
When she was 17.

540
00:33:02.213 --> 00:33:06.352
I ain't never seen
someone more alive.

541
00:33:07.153 --> 00:33:09.820
I remember driving past
this park in Amarillo.

542
00:33:09.921 --> 00:33:12.657
all these sports fields.

543
00:33:14.625 --> 00:33:17.528
Kids playing soccer
on one and...

544
00:33:17.628 --> 00:33:19.730
football on another.

545
00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:23.451
And on one field.

546
00:33:23.535 --> 00:33:26.038
all the sprinklers were running.

547
00:33:27.038 --> 00:33:30.241
It was August
and hotter than hell.

548
00:33:32.911 --> 00:33:36.714
And all those sprinklers
made a rainbow above them.

549
00:33:39.384 --> 00:33:42.387
She shouts. "Stop the car!"
[chuckles]

550
00:33:43.755 --> 00:33:45.790
And she leaps out

551
00:33:45.891 --> 00:33:48.594
and races through
those sprinklers...

552
00:33:49.528 --> 00:33:54.532
...chasing a rainbow
and dancing beneath it.

553
00:33:56.902 --> 00:33:59.337
Soaked from head to toe.

554
00:34:00.571 --> 00:34:04.442
It was the most beguiling thing
I'd ever seen.

555
00:34:05.743 --> 00:34:07.979
Someone that free.

556
00:34:13.085 --> 00:34:14.452
But...

557
00:34:16.887 --> 00:34:18.873
...demons run faster
than rainbows.

558
00:34:18.956 --> 00:34:21.427
and hers caught up to her.

559
00:34:26.164 --> 00:34:27.965
I spent 60 years

560
00:34:28.065 --> 00:34:30.969
waiting for her rainbow
to return.

561
00:34:31.802 --> 00:34:33.539
It never did.

562
00:34:35.306 --> 00:34:37.108
But that's life.

563
00:34:38.244 --> 00:34:43.449
And I wasted mine on hope.

564
00:34:49.054 --> 00:34:51.322
♪ Somber. atmospheric music ♪

565
00:35:05.237 --> 00:35:07.438
♪♪♪

566
00:35:16.514 --> 00:35:18.516
Go say goodbye to him.

567
00:35:18.617 --> 00:35:20.469
I said goodbye to him
years ago. honey.

568
00:35:20.552 --> 00:35:22.853
You need to hear
the story he just told us.

569
00:35:22.987 --> 00:35:24.572
Oh. the one about
dancing with rainbows?

570
00:35:24.655 --> 00:35:26.724
I've heard the story. babe.

571
00:35:26.824 --> 00:35:29.244
[sighs]

572
00:35:29.327 --> 00:35:31.061
Let's go. Come on.

573
00:35:33.431 --> 00:35:36.367
♪♪♪

574
00:35:36.467 --> 00:35:38.369
Thank you.

575
00:35:39.170 --> 00:35:41.873
Good luck. man. Take care.

576
00:35:42.173 --> 00:35:46.844
♪♪♪

577
00:35:46.978 --> 00:35:48.630
[Tommy]
Hey. Cooper?

578
00:35:48.713 --> 00:35:51.099
-We still got to talk. bud.
-I'll call you tomorrow.

579
00:35:51.182 --> 00:35:52.751
No. don't call. Come by.

580
00:35:54.152 --> 00:35:56.222
-Love you. Mom.
-Love you.

581
00:35:56.355 --> 00:35:58.889
-[car doors opening. closing]
-Bye.

582
00:36:06.130 --> 00:36:07.199
What?

583
00:36:07.298 --> 00:36:09.367
I think I understand you
better now.

584
00:36:10.202 --> 00:36:11.487
Well. if you don't mind
explaining me to me.

585
00:36:11.570 --> 00:36:13.170
-I'm all ears.
-Oh. I plan to.

586
00:36:13.271 --> 00:36:16.275
-[car doors opening. closing]
-[engines starting]

587
00:36:34.659 --> 00:36:36.795
♪♪♪

588
00:36:40.097 --> 00:36:42.833
[train whistling]

589
00:36:42.934 --> 00:36:45.670
♪ "Time Bomb"
by Whiskey Myers playing ♪

590
00:36:47.405 --> 00:36:50.175
♪ Yeah ♪

591
00:36:58.115 --> 00:36:59.467
-[whooping]
-♪ My head's pounding ♪

592
00:36:59.550 --> 00:37:00.668
♪ As the kick drum's drowning ♪

593
00:37:00.751 --> 00:37:02.588
♪ Everything I got left ♪

594
00:37:02.688 --> 00:37:03.838
♪ To say... ♪

595
00:37:03.922 --> 00:37:06.925
Okay. don't-don't...
don't waste it.

596
00:37:07.025 --> 00:37:09.043
-[laughs]
-Shit.

597
00:37:09.126 --> 00:37:10.929
-Hold it straight.
-Oh. yeah.

598
00:37:11.028 --> 00:37:13.097
Hold it straight.

599
00:37:13.898 --> 00:37:16.434
Shit! Fucking hell.

600
00:37:16.534 --> 00:37:18.235
What the fuck was that?

601
00:37:18.336 --> 00:37:21.539
This is absolutely
fucking terrifying.

602
00:37:21.639 --> 00:37:24.175
-[shrieking]
-♪ As above. so below ♪

603
00:37:24.275 --> 00:37:26.061
-♪ Praying for another ♪
-Oh!

604
00:37:26.143 --> 00:37:28.880
♪ Day ♪

605
00:37:28.980 --> 00:37:31.650
♪ Like a time bomb ♪

606
00:37:34.619 --> 00:37:35.954
[laughs]

607
00:37:36.086 --> 00:37:37.155
Whoo!

608
00:37:37.289 --> 00:37:39.858
♪ Yeah ♪

609
00:37:47.666 --> 00:37:50.936
♪ gentle. atmospheric music ♪

610
00:38:10.088 --> 00:38:11.657
[sighs]

611
00:38:15.025 --> 00:38:16.628
Car's waiting outside.

612
00:38:16.728 --> 00:38:18.262
I'm gonna list the house.

613
00:38:18.364 --> 00:38:19.498
-This house?
-Yep.

614
00:38:19.597 --> 00:38:20.965
Call Martha Williams

615
00:38:21.065 --> 00:38:23.335
at Williams-True
and ask her to come out.

616
00:38:24.168 --> 00:38:26.338
♪♪♪

617
00:38:28.273 --> 00:38:30.007
[Tony]
Evening. Mrs. Miller.

618
00:38:30.141 --> 00:38:32.010
-Welcome back.
-How are you. Tony?

619
00:38:32.143 --> 00:38:33.844
Good. Please. this way.

620
00:38:33.978 --> 00:38:35.347
Okay.

621
00:38:38.684 --> 00:38:40.302
I have y'all
in the corner over here.

622
00:38:40.385 --> 00:38:41.652
[Cami]
Okay.

623
00:38:41.753 --> 00:38:43.606
-[indistinct chatter]
-[soft laughter]

624
00:38:43.688 --> 00:38:45.289
Grabó su nombre.

625
00:38:45.391 --> 00:38:47.291
Ha scritto suo nome.

626
00:38:47.393 --> 00:38:48.893
-Sí.
-Ah! Hello.

627
00:38:49.027 --> 00:38:50.161
Oh.

628
00:38:50.260 --> 00:38:52.364
-Hello. new best friend.
-How are you?

629
00:38:52.498 --> 00:38:53.898
I'm good.

630
00:38:54.032 --> 00:38:55.501
-How are you?
-Very well.

631
00:38:55.601 --> 00:38:57.168
Hello. Cami. How are you?

632
00:38:57.268 --> 00:38:58.570
Good to see you.

633
00:38:58.670 --> 00:39:00.088
I hope you don't mind
my wife joining. Here.

634
00:39:00.170 --> 00:39:01.556
She gets very jealous
when I'm dining alone

635
00:39:01.639 --> 00:39:03.326
-with beautiful women.
-Please. I wish

636
00:39:03.409 --> 00:39:06.094
I had joined my husband on a few
more of his business dinners.

637
00:39:06.177 --> 00:39:08.045
More than you know.

638
00:39:08.146 --> 00:39:09.565
-Thank you.
-I took the liberty

639
00:39:09.648 --> 00:39:11.416
of ordering you a tequila.

640
00:39:11.516 --> 00:39:13.217
Ooh. wow. Good memory.

641
00:39:13.318 --> 00:39:15.838
My wife has the memory. I just
have the good sense to ask her.

642
00:39:15.920 --> 00:39:18.340
[Bella] Do you want me to sit at
the bar and let you talk shop?

643
00:39:18.423 --> 00:39:21.126
I don't know. how big of a shop
are we talking?

644
00:39:21.226 --> 00:39:22.226
It's big.

645
00:39:22.360 --> 00:39:24.829
-Okay.
-Yeah.

646
00:39:24.929 --> 00:39:26.414
All right.
We'll solve the world's problems

647
00:39:26.498 --> 00:39:27.815
before the first course.
I promise.

648
00:39:27.898 --> 00:39:29.460
-Okay. Ciao. bello.
-Ciao. Bella.

649
00:39:29.568 --> 00:39:32.103
Let me grab the drink.

650
00:39:37.409 --> 00:39:39.376
I'm all ears.

651
00:39:43.280 --> 00:39:46.668
Your company invests
in drilling expeditions?

652
00:39:46.751 --> 00:39:49.688
We finance exploration. yes.

653
00:39:49.788 --> 00:39:52.923
-And do you have a ceiling?
-Well. everybody has a ceiling.

654
00:39:53.023 --> 00:39:54.460
but we have yet to find ours.

655
00:39:54.592 --> 00:39:57.596
Well. I need to drill
an existing well.

656
00:39:57.695 --> 00:40:01.432
It's an offshore rig that
was damaged in the hurricane.

657
00:40:01.532 --> 00:40:02.900
In the gulf?

658
00:40:03.001 --> 00:40:05.335
Correct. But there's no risk.

659
00:40:05.436 --> 00:40:06.855
It's an existing gas field.

660
00:40:06.938 --> 00:40:09.775
and the location's
been thoroughly mapped.

661
00:40:09.875 --> 00:40:12.143
The challenge isn't
in finding the gas.

662
00:40:12.277 --> 00:40:13.896
it's getting to it.

663
00:40:13.978 --> 00:40:17.114
And the challenge with that
is the time it takes.

664
00:40:17.215 --> 00:40:18.867
What's the timeline?

665
00:40:18.949 --> 00:40:20.652
If we start drilling in 90 days.

666
00:40:20.751 --> 00:40:23.954
we should reach the field
in about ten months.

667
00:40:24.755 --> 00:40:26.992
-And what's the loan amount?
-I'd say

668
00:40:27.092 --> 00:40:30.596
$325 to $350 million.

669
00:40:33.599 --> 00:40:36.083
Isn't this something that Tommy
should be negotiating?

670
00:40:36.166 --> 00:40:38.586
Well. it's my company.

671
00:40:38.670 --> 00:40:40.472
I'll be paying the note.

672
00:40:40.572 --> 00:40:43.041
I should be negotiating it.

673
00:40:47.646 --> 00:40:50.447
Your husband. he left you
quite a mess. didn't he?

674
00:40:54.820 --> 00:40:57.355
It wasn't intentional.

675
00:40:59.690 --> 00:41:01.992
But yes. he did.

676
00:41:07.699 --> 00:41:09.800
Snakes are cannibals.
Did you know that?

677
00:41:09.900 --> 00:41:12.103
I did not.

678
00:41:12.202 --> 00:41:16.875
They eat rabbits.
mice. squirrels. quail.

679
00:41:17.007 --> 00:41:19.376
But they also eat each other.

680
00:41:19.476 --> 00:41:22.648
I know my business is similar.

681
00:41:22.748 --> 00:41:26.818
But the snakes. we have a code.

682
00:41:26.918 --> 00:41:28.987
We only eat other snakes.

683
00:41:29.086 --> 00:41:33.891
No rabbits. no mice. no quail.

684
00:41:35.126 --> 00:41:38.228
I'd like to help you.
but I can't negotiate with you.

685
00:41:38.329 --> 00:41:40.565
Not because you're a woman.

686
00:41:41.599 --> 00:41:43.268
You're not a snake.

687
00:41:44.068 --> 00:41:46.103
Have Tommy reach out.

688
00:41:46.871 --> 00:41:48.907
Are you calling Tommy a snake?

689
00:41:49.039 --> 00:41:51.509
Well. maybe not a snake.
but. uh.

690
00:41:51.610 --> 00:41:53.744
he's a hawk.

691
00:41:53.878 --> 00:41:55.413
And hawks?

692
00:41:56.213 --> 00:41:58.349
They eat snakes. too.

693
00:41:59.851 --> 00:42:01.251
[dish clatters softly]

694
00:42:05.056 --> 00:42:06.423
Thank you.

695
00:42:07.324 --> 00:42:08.309
Thank you.

696
00:42:08.393 --> 00:42:10.144
Don't you worry about a thing.

697
00:42:10.228 --> 00:42:12.030
The answer is yes.

698
00:42:12.130 --> 00:42:14.431
I'll let the snakes
figure out the rest.

699
00:42:16.034 --> 00:42:17.318
You drank your drink already?

700
00:42:17.402 --> 00:42:19.536
-Uh. maybe.
-[Cami laughs]

701
00:42:19.637 --> 00:42:20.905
[laughter]

702
00:42:21.005 --> 00:42:23.074
It's gonna be a long night.

703
00:42:27.746 --> 00:42:30.014
♪ Slow. atmospheric music ♪

704
00:42:44.429 --> 00:42:47.599
[Ariana] Don't know
how you turned out so kind.

705
00:42:47.733 --> 00:42:49.701
[Cooper]
I don't know about "kind."

706
00:42:49.800 --> 00:42:53.137
I try to do what's right.
what's decent.

707
00:42:53.237 --> 00:42:55.773
Don't always do it. but I try.

708
00:42:55.873 --> 00:43:00.210
[laughs softly]
Like I said. kind.

709
00:43:11.889 --> 00:43:14.041
Would you like to come inside?

710
00:43:14.125 --> 00:43:16.293
-You okay with that?
-[chuckles]

711
00:43:16.393 --> 00:43:18.096
I didn't ask you
to jump in my bed.

712
00:43:18.195 --> 00:43:21.065
I asked if you would like
to come inside.

713
00:43:22.900 --> 00:43:24.001
I would like that.

714
00:43:24.135 --> 00:43:25.503
[Ariana laughs softly]

715
00:43:29.074 --> 00:43:30.474
[engine turns off]

716
00:43:38.182 --> 00:43:39.751
[door closes]

717
00:43:46.925 --> 00:43:48.293
My house.

718
00:43:49.927 --> 00:43:51.295
I know.

719
00:43:52.429 --> 00:43:54.666
It's not much. but it's mine.

720
00:43:55.465 --> 00:43:57.668
And I like it.

721
00:44:00.304 --> 00:44:02.606
Miguel's abuelita's house.

722
00:44:02.708 --> 00:44:05.811
Down the street. his tíos. tías.

723
00:44:05.911 --> 00:44:07.545
Sus primos.

724
00:44:07.679 --> 00:44:09.914
They're all right here.

725
00:44:10.782 --> 00:44:12.217
Having met your family.

726
00:44:12.349 --> 00:44:13.936
I can understand
why being close to them

727
00:44:14.018 --> 00:44:15.920
is not a priority of yours.

728
00:44:17.322 --> 00:44:19.190
But it's everything to me.

729
00:44:20.826 --> 00:44:22.476
And I will work.

730
00:44:22.559 --> 00:44:24.112
You might not like the job.
but it doesn't matter

731
00:44:24.195 --> 00:44:26.396
'cause you're
not the one doing it.

732
00:44:27.699 --> 00:44:29.900
And next time I kick you out.

733
00:44:30.001 --> 00:44:32.838
you don't just leave
and stay gone.

734
00:44:32.938 --> 00:44:36.206
You figure out why I did it.
fix it...

735
00:44:36.974 --> 00:44:40.378
...and then come home
and tell me how sorry you are.

736
00:44:42.547 --> 00:44:45.182
I'm sorry I...

737
00:44:45.282 --> 00:44:47.485
struck oil and got rich.

738
00:44:47.585 --> 00:44:49.755
-I-I won't let it happen again.
-[laughs]

739
00:44:51.088 --> 00:44:53.724
-You're on real thin ice. flaco.
-I know.

740
00:44:53.858 --> 00:44:55.510
Um...

741
00:44:55.592 --> 00:44:57.061
I am sorry.

742
00:44:57.195 --> 00:45:00.148
I didn't ask
for your dreams or...

743
00:45:00.231 --> 00:45:01.784
which ones
I should make come true

744
00:45:01.867 --> 00:45:04.068
and which ones
should just stay dreams.

745
00:45:04.202 --> 00:45:06.271
You can't make
my dreams come true.

746
00:45:06.371 --> 00:45:08.572
Only I can do that.

747
00:45:10.208 --> 00:45:11.576
Got it?

748
00:45:12.911 --> 00:45:14.644
Got it.

749
00:45:15.780 --> 00:45:17.148
Okay.

750
00:45:19.885 --> 00:45:22.152
♪ Soft. hopeful music ♪

751
00:45:23.954 --> 00:45:25.990
This is very confusing.

752
00:45:26.090 --> 00:45:27.425
[laughs softly]
I know.

753
00:45:27.557 --> 00:45:29.626
It's confusing to me. too.

754
00:45:32.764 --> 00:45:34.900
I want to buy you
a new dishwasher.

755
00:45:35.766 --> 00:45:37.268
[both laugh]

756
00:45:39.204 --> 00:45:41.056
-Okay. fine.
-No. really.

757
00:45:41.139 --> 00:45:43.708
Can we at least take
a trip or something?

758
00:45:44.608 --> 00:45:46.476
Trip where?

759
00:45:46.610 --> 00:45:49.646
I don't know.
Where do you want to go?

760
00:45:49.746 --> 00:45:53.885
Hmm. You might
just figure this out.

761
00:45:53.985 --> 00:45:56.153
It's pretty simple.
All I got to do is

762
00:45:56.286 --> 00:45:58.489
ask you everything.

763
00:45:59.590 --> 00:46:02.827
Hmm. My God.
he did figure it out.

764
00:46:03.994 --> 00:46:05.630
Okay. now you can jump
in my bed.

765
00:46:05.762 --> 00:46:07.331
[laughs]

766
00:46:08.132 --> 00:46:10.335
♪♪♪

767
00:46:18.376 --> 00:46:20.411
♪ soft. somber music ♪

768
00:46:42.032 --> 00:46:43.717
Patient suffered traumatic
transhumeral amputation.

769
00:46:43.800 --> 00:46:47.371
A.E. right side. BP 98/54.

770
00:46:47.505 --> 00:46:49.206
-HR 122.
-Car wreck?

771
00:46:49.306 --> 00:46:51.358
Rig. Caught his arm
beneath the hydraulic shaft.

772
00:46:51.442 --> 00:46:53.077
Put him in three. Let's go.

773
00:46:56.146 --> 00:46:57.916
He's awake.

774
00:46:59.951 --> 00:47:02.152
[indistinct chatter]

775
00:47:07.858 --> 00:47:09.911
[doctor] ...certain amount
of tissue damage to the area.

776
00:47:09.994 --> 00:47:11.346
And that's going to have
some other complications

777
00:47:11.429 --> 00:47:12.730
further down the line.

778
00:47:12.829 --> 00:47:15.867
So. what he's currently
dealing with

779
00:47:15.967 --> 00:47:19.204
is severe ocular inflammation

780
00:47:19.304 --> 00:47:21.907
and severe
pulmonary inflammation.

781
00:47:22.039 --> 00:47:23.425
Now. what we don't know
at this point

782
00:47:23.507 --> 00:47:25.460
is whether this damage
is permanent.

783
00:47:25.543 --> 00:47:26.911
His breathing is improved.

784
00:47:27.012 --> 00:47:28.831
Once the ocular inflammation
is down.

785
00:47:28.914 --> 00:47:31.099
we'll look at what
neurological damage may persist.

786
00:47:31.181 --> 00:47:32.699
When you. when you say
"neurological." you're...

787
00:47:32.782 --> 00:47:34.552
Memory issues. cognitive issues.

788
00:47:34.684 --> 00:47:37.806
People can lose sense
of taste and smell.

789
00:47:37.889 --> 00:47:39.856
How is his nervous system
affected?

790
00:47:39.958 --> 00:47:41.309
Does he have full motor skills?

791
00:47:41.391 --> 00:47:43.978
Is there numbness
in his extremities?

792
00:47:44.061 --> 00:47:45.963
Only time can answer
these questions.

793
00:47:46.063 --> 00:47:47.481
-But he is talking.
-He can speak.

794
00:47:47.565 --> 00:47:49.067
He can respond when spoken to.

795
00:47:49.199 --> 00:47:51.268
Does he have family close?

796
00:47:51.402 --> 00:47:53.487
They're all in Houston.

797
00:47:53.570 --> 00:47:56.074
He's gonna need his family.

798
00:47:56.173 --> 00:47:57.492
Can we see him?

799
00:47:57.574 --> 00:47:59.344
Uh. he just
regained consciousness.

800
00:47:59.443 --> 00:48:02.079
so let's keep it brief.

801
00:48:12.590 --> 00:48:14.858
Hey. how's it going. my man?

802
00:48:14.960 --> 00:48:16.927
-Boss?
-What's up?

803
00:48:17.061 --> 00:48:19.297
[King] You scared the shit
out of us. bro.

804
00:48:19.396 --> 00:48:20.715
Yeah. we thought you was dead.

805
00:48:20.797 --> 00:48:22.550
[laughs softly]
You ain't the only one.

806
00:48:22.632 --> 00:48:24.534
How you feeling. man?

807
00:48:24.635 --> 00:48:25.936
My fucking eyes. man.

808
00:48:26.070 --> 00:48:27.688
[BR] Yeah. you're one
lucky son of a bitch.

809
00:48:27.771 --> 00:48:29.791
There's dead people and animals
all around that pumpjack.

810
00:48:29.873 --> 00:48:32.443
-Yeah. We're all lucky.
-Yeah.

811
00:48:32.543 --> 00:48:34.778
[nurse]
Okay. Jerrell?

812
00:48:36.447 --> 00:48:38.115
Just gonna change your compress.

813
00:48:38.215 --> 00:48:39.916
-All right.
-Get a nice cool one

814
00:48:40.018 --> 00:48:42.487
-on there. Okay?
-Yeah.

815
00:48:43.487 --> 00:48:45.690
Head up. There we go.

816
00:48:51.128 --> 00:48:52.730
How come I can't see?

817
00:48:54.798 --> 00:48:55.884
You took it off. right?

818
00:48:55.967 --> 00:48:57.251
Just keep your eyes closed. hon.

819
00:48:57.335 --> 00:48:59.670
But-but... Hey.
How come I can't see?

820
00:48:59.804 --> 00:49:01.972
-It's all right.
-I'll send in the doctor.

821
00:49:02.072 --> 00:49:04.976
-Hey. Boss. Boss. Boss.
-Hey. Yeah. I'm-I'm right here.

822
00:49:05.076 --> 00:49:06.527
-I'm here. I'm right here. man.
-I can't fucking see.

823
00:49:06.610 --> 00:49:08.646
Your eyes.
they're inflamed. okay?

824
00:49:08.746 --> 00:49:10.731
They're puffy and they have...
have fluid coming out.

825
00:49:10.815 --> 00:49:12.434
Th-That's why you can't see.
that's what the doctor said.

826
00:49:12.516 --> 00:49:13.784
so...

827
00:49:13.884 --> 00:49:15.619
Did-did he say I'm-a see again?

828
00:49:15.719 --> 00:49:17.422
♪ Slow. somber music ♪

829
00:49:17.521 --> 00:49:19.606
I ain't no doctor.
but I-I'll go get him.

830
00:49:19.690 --> 00:49:21.226
[Jerrell]
Wait. Boss.

831
00:49:21.326 --> 00:49:23.144
How the fuck's a man supposed
to take care of his family

832
00:49:23.228 --> 00:49:24.362
if he can't see?

833
00:49:24.461 --> 00:49:25.947
You know how many mouths
I got to feed.

834
00:49:26.030 --> 00:49:27.414
Yeah. I do. I do.
Let me go get the doctor.

835
00:49:27.498 --> 00:49:29.833
-Doctor! Doctor!
-Jerrell.

836
00:49:29.934 --> 00:49:31.085
-I'm-a go get him.
-Man. doctor!

837
00:49:31.168 --> 00:49:33.503
-Man. relax.
-Doctor! Doctor!

838
00:49:33.637 --> 00:49:35.005
Doctor! Doctor!

839
00:49:35.106 --> 00:49:36.590
[woman over P.A.]
Rapid response. ICU 11.

840
00:49:36.673 --> 00:49:38.143
Rapid response.

841
00:49:38.242 --> 00:49:41.112
Rapid response. ICU 11.
Rapid response.

842
00:49:41.378 --> 00:49:43.547
♪♪♪

843
00:49:49.454 --> 00:49:50.855
[soft crying]

844
00:50:10.840 --> 00:50:12.577
Hey. baby. what's wrong?

845
00:50:15.846 --> 00:50:17.465
[sniffles]

846
00:50:17.547 --> 00:50:20.050
You save her life.

847
00:50:20.150 --> 00:50:24.621
and then
she kicks you in the face.

848
00:50:26.056 --> 00:50:28.492
Who does that to their child?

849
00:50:30.027 --> 00:50:32.429
I don't care
how many rainbows she chased.

850
00:50:32.530 --> 00:50:35.599
I hope God takes
one of those rainbows

851
00:50:35.699 --> 00:50:38.603
and just shoves it
right up her ass.

852
00:50:44.675 --> 00:50:46.661
Honey. my mother

853
00:50:46.744 --> 00:50:50.315
was far away
from gods and rainbows.

854
00:50:51.949 --> 00:50:55.253
That ain't where she went.
honey. if you know what I mean.

855
00:50:56.621 --> 00:50:58.088
[softly]
Yeah.

856
00:50:58.188 --> 00:51:01.425
But I'm gonna tell you something
that might help explain it.

857
00:51:05.630 --> 00:51:07.898
I had a sister.

858
00:51:09.065 --> 00:51:10.835
And. uh...

859
00:51:12.036 --> 00:51:15.672
...she died from SIDS
at four months old.

860
00:51:16.474 --> 00:51:17.675
What is that?

861
00:51:17.775 --> 00:51:19.643
It's when a baby dies
in his sleep

862
00:51:19.744 --> 00:51:20.945
and they don't know why.

863
00:51:21.077 --> 00:51:24.565
It. uh. maybe it rolled
on its stomach or.

864
00:51:24.648 --> 00:51:26.068
you know. the little lungs

865
00:51:26.150 --> 00:51:28.536
couldn't get enough air.
you know.

866
00:51:28.619 --> 00:51:30.320
-[exhales]
-Nobody knows. honey.

867
00:51:30.454 --> 00:51:31.873
[sniffles]

868
00:51:31.956 --> 00:51:33.490
But. uh...

869
00:51:33.623 --> 00:51:35.693
Well. the loss broke her.

870
00:51:35.793 --> 00:51:40.231
and. uh. it just
snapped her in two.

871
00:51:41.065 --> 00:51:44.835
I think she was just so scared

872
00:51:44.969 --> 00:51:49.056
to feel any kind of love again
after that that...

873
00:51:49.139 --> 00:51:53.244
that she drugged and drank
her soul to death.

874
00:51:53.344 --> 00:51:54.844
That's not an excuse.

875
00:51:54.945 --> 00:51:57.164
Well. sweetie.
I didn't say I could justify it.

876
00:51:57.248 --> 00:52:00.184
I-I just said I'll explain it.
that's all.

877
00:52:00.318 --> 00:52:02.320
What. you think
she was hard on me?

878
00:52:02.420 --> 00:52:06.324
My poor father. he...
he was scared to death of her.

879
00:52:06.423 --> 00:52:09.494
He would spend a whole year
at a camp...

880
00:52:10.827 --> 00:52:13.130
...and not come home once.

881
00:52:13.998 --> 00:52:16.201
Just send the checks.

882
00:52:17.768 --> 00:52:20.670
He wasted his life
hiding from her.

883
00:52:20.771 --> 00:52:23.507
That's so tragic.

884
00:52:23.641 --> 00:52:25.376
Yeah.

885
00:52:25.510 --> 00:52:28.179
But it's my tragedy. honey.
not yours.

886
00:52:28.278 --> 00:52:30.447
-Okay?
-Okay.

887
00:52:30.547 --> 00:52:32.016
♪ Slow. somber music ♪

888
00:52:32.115 --> 00:52:34.818
I have to say. there's not
many people on this planet

889
00:52:34.918 --> 00:52:37.188
that care enough
to cry over something

890
00:52:37.288 --> 00:52:40.724
that somebody else went through.

891
00:52:42.626 --> 00:52:46.297
You got a big old heart
beating under that hood. baby.

892
00:52:47.565 --> 00:52:49.867
[whispers]
I got it from you.

893
00:52:57.641 --> 00:53:00.077
-Love you.
-Love you. baby.

894
00:53:03.648 --> 00:53:05.782
♪♪♪

895
00:53:12.822 --> 00:53:14.775
I've lived through some
heart-wrenching fucking days

896
00:53:14.858 --> 00:53:17.494
in my life. Tommy. but this one?

897
00:53:17.594 --> 00:53:19.313
[sighs]
Here we go.

898
00:53:19.396 --> 00:53:20.864
I swear. Tommy.

899
00:53:20.965 --> 00:53:23.650
Like. of all the calamities
that I have endured...

900
00:53:23.733 --> 00:53:25.320
Now. what calamity
are we talking about now?

901
00:53:25.402 --> 00:53:28.672
The great sunscreen shortage
of 2007?

902
00:53:28.773 --> 00:53:30.440
How about our marriage?

903
00:53:30.541 --> 00:53:32.193
[chuckles]
We solved that. didn't we?

904
00:53:32.277 --> 00:53:33.661
I mean. I don't see
a ring on my finger.

905
00:53:33.744 --> 00:53:36.246
I do. Are we not calling
those little shiny things

906
00:53:36.380 --> 00:53:38.615
that reflect on the ceiling
"rings" anymore?

907
00:53:38.748 --> 00:53:40.918
This is from our first marriage.

908
00:53:41.050 --> 00:53:42.619
All right? It doesn't count.

909
00:53:42.753 --> 00:53:44.054
It's tainted.

910
00:53:44.153 --> 00:53:45.539
Well. give it back to me.

911
00:53:45.623 --> 00:53:47.608
I'll trade the son of a bitch in
and buy a new truck.

912
00:53:47.692 --> 00:53:49.193
[scoffs]
Shit.

913
00:53:49.293 --> 00:53:50.945
You know. there are
so many things about our lives

914
00:53:51.027 --> 00:53:54.130
that need to be fixed.
and do you know where it starts?

915
00:53:54.264 --> 00:53:55.617
[quietly]
This ought to be good.

916
00:53:55.699 --> 00:53:57.385
No. where does it start. honey?

917
00:53:57.467 --> 00:53:59.436
Where it always starts.

918
00:53:59.536 --> 00:54:01.672
The beginning.

919
00:54:02.472 --> 00:54:05.041
I'm not following you.

920
00:54:06.911 --> 00:54:08.746
Your father.

921
00:54:08.846 --> 00:54:11.114
He's rotting away
in some miserable excuse

922
00:54:11.215 --> 00:54:13.650
for a nursing home with nobody.

923
00:54:14.784 --> 00:54:17.086
Nobody loves him.

924
00:54:17.186 --> 00:54:18.405
That was his choice.

925
00:54:18.489 --> 00:54:20.324
You can't be a father
to our children

926
00:54:20.458 --> 00:54:22.492
if you can't be a son to him.

927
00:54:22.626 --> 00:54:24.911
Okay. two things: first of all.

928
00:54:24.994 --> 00:54:28.065
stop watching those
fucking daytime talk shows.

929
00:54:28.164 --> 00:54:31.436
And second of all.
our kids are grown.

930
00:54:31.536 --> 00:54:33.804
Job done. They're adults.

931
00:54:33.903 --> 00:54:36.507
Tommy. my life
is with old folks.

932
00:54:36.641 --> 00:54:39.594
Okay? And no matter who
they were when they were young.

933
00:54:39.677 --> 00:54:44.280
now that they're old. I mean.
every regret. every mistake...

934
00:54:45.014 --> 00:54:47.302
...they have chewed them up
and mulled them over.

935
00:54:47.385 --> 00:54:49.186
and they are sorry.

936
00:54:50.019 --> 00:54:53.324
I mean. they're deeply.
deeply sorry.

937
00:54:54.324 --> 00:54:56.760
I mean. he deserves peace.

938
00:55:01.699 --> 00:55:04.952
And you're the only one
who can give that to him.

939
00:55:05.034 --> 00:55:07.237
How am I gonna do that?

940
00:55:07.338 --> 00:55:09.139
Um...

941
00:55:20.351 --> 00:55:22.387
Why did you close the door?

942
00:55:23.186 --> 00:55:26.391
So you don't wake
the whole house when I tell you.

943
00:55:26.523 --> 00:55:29.559
♪ Slow. atmospheric music ♪

944
00:55:30.795 --> 00:55:33.630
[Tommy] Are you out
of your fucking mind?

945
00:55:36.166 --> 00:55:38.268
[radio DJ 1]
Good morning. Permian Basin.

946
00:55:38.369 --> 00:55:41.188
If you've got a swimming pool.
today is the day to get in it.

947
00:55:41.271 --> 00:55:42.789
[radio DJ 2] I'd fill it
with ice cubes first.

948
00:55:42.873 --> 00:55:44.224
[radio DJ 1]
102. the expected high today.

949
00:55:44.307 --> 00:55:45.693
[radio DJ 2]
Summer came early.

950
00:55:45.775 --> 00:55:47.329
and when summer comes
to West Texas.

951
00:55:47.411 --> 00:55:49.380
-it stays.
-Till November.

952
00:55:49.480 --> 00:55:51.065
[radio DJ 2] So. if you've
got things to do outside.

953
00:55:51.148 --> 00:55:53.134
-you better get to them.
-Stop wasting time.

954
00:55:53.217 --> 00:55:54.936
-[DJ 2] Stop it right now.
-That's the theme

955
00:55:55.018 --> 00:55:56.903
of the day.
and here's a song to go with it.

956
00:55:56.987 --> 00:55:58.355
from The Red Clay Strays.

957
00:55:58.456 --> 00:56:00.824
["Wasting Time"
by The Red Clay Strays playing]

958
00:56:11.969 --> 00:56:14.170
[song playing over radio]

959
00:56:16.039 --> 00:56:18.943
♪ Another year around the sun.
and nothing's been done ♪

960
00:56:19.043 --> 00:56:22.447
♪ I got to get out
of this state I'm in ♪

961
00:56:22.547 --> 00:56:25.416
♪ My wheels have been spinning.
but I ain't been moving ♪

962
00:56:25.516 --> 00:56:28.369
♪ Got to get back
on the track again ♪

963
00:56:28.452 --> 00:56:30.420
♪ I've been stuck in a rut ♪

964
00:56:30.554 --> 00:56:32.172
♪ Just a-kicking up mud ♪

965
00:56:32.255 --> 00:56:34.759
♪ And I'm sick of waiting
round for the change ♪

966
00:56:35.860 --> 00:56:39.096
♪ I got my foot on the gas.
gonna make things happen ♪

967
00:56:39.228 --> 00:56:41.599
♪ And do them all my own way ♪

968
00:56:43.067 --> 00:56:45.887
♪ Can't wait. won't waste ♪

969
00:56:45.969 --> 00:56:49.539
♪ Ain't wasting time
no more... ♪

970
00:56:49.639 --> 00:56:51.108
-[sighs]
-[toilet flushes]

971
00:56:51.208 --> 00:56:52.777
Oh. God.

972
00:56:56.547 --> 00:56:59.449
-Hi.
-Morning.

973
00:57:04.454 --> 00:57:05.822
Okay.

974
00:57:05.922 --> 00:57:07.692
You need a ride to your car?

975
00:57:08.458 --> 00:57:10.327
No. uh. I'll just...

976
00:57:10.427 --> 00:57:12.146
call an Uber once
I've gathered up my dignity.

977
00:57:12.228 --> 00:57:14.164
[chuckles]
Oh. come on.

978
00:57:14.297 --> 00:57:16.266
Don't do that. Don't regret it.

979
00:57:16.365 --> 00:57:17.534
I had a lot of fun.

980
00:57:17.635 --> 00:57:19.469
-I'm sure you did.
-[laughs softly]

981
00:57:19.570 --> 00:57:21.588
You're gonna pretend
like you don't remember?

982
00:57:21.672 --> 00:57:23.907
-No.
-No?

983
00:57:24.007 --> 00:57:25.675
No. it's all coming back to me.

984
00:57:25.775 --> 00:57:27.644
[chuckles]

985
00:57:27.777 --> 00:57:29.230
Mind if I use your shower?

986
00:57:29.313 --> 00:57:31.181
What's mine is yours. love.

987
00:57:31.280 --> 00:57:32.817
Thank you.

988
00:57:34.719 --> 00:57:36.320
[sniffles]

989
00:57:38.523 --> 00:57:41.592
You do know I saw it all
last night. right?

990
00:57:41.692 --> 00:57:43.860
Yeah. well. it was dark
last night. so...

991
00:57:45.161 --> 00:57:46.771
Looks pretty good
in the day. too.

992
00:57:47.965 --> 00:57:50.800
I'm so glad you think so.

993
00:57:52.168 --> 00:57:53.903
[exhales]

994
00:58:03.681 --> 00:58:05.432
-[knocking on door]
-Yes?

995
00:58:05.516 --> 00:58:09.152
[Charlie] Hey. it's me.
Remember. from the bedroom?

996
00:58:10.387 --> 00:58:11.588
-Hi.
-Hi.

997
00:58:11.688 --> 00:58:14.190
Oh. towels.
You need fresh towels.

998
00:58:14.291 --> 00:58:17.360
Right in the cabinet over there.
the far right cabinet.

999
00:58:17.494 --> 00:58:19.195
-Great. Thanks.
-Cool.

1000
00:58:19.295 --> 00:58:21.030
Okay. What?

1001
00:58:21.130 --> 00:58:23.867
Look. it's too early
and I'm too hungover

1002
00:58:24.001 --> 00:58:25.202
for you to be charming.

1003
00:58:25.335 --> 00:58:27.288
Okay. fine. I'll just. uh.

1004
00:58:27.371 --> 00:58:30.273
I'll call you later
and be charming then.

1005
00:58:31.141 --> 00:58:32.577
-Great.
-Cool.

1006
00:58:33.878 --> 00:58:35.746
You know.
there's a body oil in there

1007
00:58:35.846 --> 00:58:38.949
that is. uh. pretty good.
you should try it out.

1008
00:58:39.048 --> 00:58:40.333
-Thank you.
-Oh. you know.

1009
00:58:40.416 --> 00:58:42.637
and the aromatherapy discs
are pretty good.

1010
00:58:42.719 --> 00:58:44.137
You just throw them on the drain

1011
00:58:44.221 --> 00:58:45.639
-and you like...
-I got it from here.

1012
00:58:45.722 --> 00:58:47.023
It's not my first shower.

1013
00:58:47.123 --> 00:58:48.257
Oh. it's not? Okay.

1014
00:58:48.358 --> 00:58:49.610
Well. I'm-I'm in a rush.
I've got to run.

1015
00:58:49.693 --> 00:58:51.144
-Okay.
-Yeah. I'll call you later.

1016
00:58:51.228 --> 00:58:53.362
-Can't wait.
-Good.

1017
00:58:58.869 --> 00:59:00.536
[water running]

1018
00:59:14.918 --> 00:59:16.920
[sighs]

1019
00:59:17.021 --> 00:59:18.387
Okay.

1020
00:59:18.487 --> 00:59:22.126
Aroma therapy pod. nice touch.

1021
00:59:22.226 --> 00:59:24.094
♪ Soft. atmospheric music ♪

1022
00:59:49.452 --> 00:59:51.621
♪♪♪

1023
01:00:12.342 --> 01:00:14.043
What are you doing here?

1024
01:00:15.945 --> 01:00:18.382
Ignoring my better judgment.

1025
01:00:19.583 --> 01:00:22.585
'Cause that's what
pleasing my wife requires.

1026
01:00:24.487 --> 01:00:27.190
You're here to please your wife?

1027
01:00:27.291 --> 01:00:28.858
Yeah. I am.

1028
01:00:29.960 --> 01:00:32.228
And what would it take
to do that?

1029
01:00:32.329 --> 01:00:34.331
Having you in our lives again...

1030
01:00:35.132 --> 01:00:36.617
...getting to know
your grandkids

1031
01:00:36.701 --> 01:00:38.835
and getting to know her.

1032
01:00:40.469 --> 01:00:43.072
I'm pretty used up. son.

1033
01:00:45.009 --> 01:00:47.210
Yeah. so am I. Pop.

1034
01:00:48.512 --> 01:00:50.880
So. what's the plan?

1035
01:00:51.882 --> 01:00:55.518
You move me to a home closer
and just forget about me there?

1036
01:00:55.652 --> 01:00:59.923
No. actually. we're thinking
about bringing you home.

1037
01:01:03.893 --> 01:01:06.530
Listen. Pop. I'm not
gonna try too hard at this.

1038
01:01:06.630 --> 01:01:08.965
If you want to stay out here
and die. fine.

1039
01:01:09.065 --> 01:01:10.918
Or you can come with me
and watch the sun

1040
01:01:11.001 --> 01:01:12.568
all damn day long.

1041
01:01:12.702 --> 01:01:15.789
You can watch it set
and sit out there all night.

1042
01:01:15.873 --> 01:01:18.909
Second chances
don't come around that often.

1043
01:01:19.675 --> 01:01:21.494
And this one ain't ever
coming around again

1044
01:01:21.577 --> 01:01:22.980
for neither one of us.

1045
01:01:25.048 --> 01:01:26.916
It's about to go.

1046
01:01:30.054 --> 01:01:32.255
♪♪♪

1047
01:01:49.039 --> 01:01:51.208
Let me go grab my things.

1048
01:01:51.307 --> 01:01:53.543
I already got them.

1049
01:01:53.643 --> 01:01:57.313
You ain't ever setting another
foot in that fucking place.

1050
01:02:02.351 --> 01:02:04.288
I'm not sure I deserve this.

1051
01:02:04.420 --> 01:02:08.125
What does deserve
have to do with it. Pop?

1052
01:02:22.106 --> 01:02:24.273
♪♪♪

1053
01:02:32.081 --> 01:02:34.284
♪ gentle music ♪
